      "message": "**Issue #1 (🔴 High Severity (MUST FIX))**: Incorrect Kernel Config Assertion in `Ssif Subsystems`\n\n**Issue**: Incorrect Kernel Config Assertion in `Ssif Subsystems`\n\n**Why**: The test executes `cat /proc/config.gz | zcat | grep SSIF` which outputs only lines containing \"SSIF\", then asserts the presence of `CONFIG_NET_PTP_CLASSIFY\u003dy`. That string has nothing to do with SSIF and would never appear in SSIF-filtered output — the assertion either always fails (correct) or the command actually returns more output than expected. The line immediately below already checks `CONFIG_SSIF_IPMI_BMC\u003dy` (line 28), so this duplicate path is either dead code or a copy/paste error. Remove line 27 or replace it with a meaningful SSIF config assertion.",
