      "message": "**Issue #3 (🟡 Medium Severity (SHOULD FIX))**: Hard-coded `Sleep  5s` Tunnel Wait with No Observable Condition\n\n**Issue**: This sleep is inserted before the `curl` tunnel-verification step but no inline comment explains why a 5-second fixed delay is necessary instead of polling.\n\n**Fix**:\n```robot\n    # Wait for the SSH tunnel process to bind the local port before sending traffic.\n    # No direct observable condition is available; 5 s is sufficient for ssh to establish the tunnel.\n    Sleep  5s\n```\n\n```robot\n    Wait Until Keyword Succeeds  15s  1s\n    ...  Run Process  curl  -k  https://127.0.0.1:18443/redfish/v1\n```\n\n**Why**: Unexplained hard-coded sleeps can mask race conditions and slow down the test unnecessarily in fast environments. If the delay cannot be eliminated, an inline comment explaining why is mandatory per project convention.",
