      "message": "**Issue #5 (🟢 Low Severity (NICE TO FIX))**: `Verify Bootstrap Account Deleted` Uses String Conversion for Membership Check\n\n**Issue**: Converting the Members list to a string and doing a substring search is fragile — if a future username happens to be a substring of an existing URI path, the check could produce a false positive or false negative. Iterating the Members list and checking `@odata.id` directly is more robust.\n\n**Fix**:\n```robot\n${uris}\u003d  Evaluate  [m[\u0027@odata.id\u0027] for m in $resp.dict[\u0027Members\u0027]]\nShould Not Contain  ${uris}  /redfish/v1/AccountService/Accounts/${BOOTSTRAP_USERNAME}\n```\n\n**Why**: Defensive test assertions are more reliable than string-contains checks on serialised data structures.",
